nodes.body:
@pos-ei-don thanks — that's exactly the validation this needed: 51 progress lines at clean 30s cadence across a 26-minute cold start, and a served completion confirming the patched path is behaviorally inert. Your phase table also puts real numbers on the default question: warmup alone (1030s, JIT-dominated) exceeds the 600s default before weight loading is even counted, and that's with ninja already throttled to the realistic `MAX_JOBS=4` for that box. I've linked your data from #48031 so the platform-aware-default discussion has it.

Also: rebased onto current main per mergify (`f6bad7d49`). Only structural change from the rebase: main gained `_wait_for_new_engine_ready` in the meantime, so instead of inlining at the call site it now delegates to the shared `_wait_for_engine_ready` — same dedupe, same messages. Tests re-run green on the rebased head.

Maintainers: this is ready for review — CPU tests + real-hardware validation from the original reporter above.

